# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED — the realtime transport
#
# Both of these are designed to be shipped to browsers. There is no secret key
# anywhere in this app; if a feature ever needed one, it was not built.
# Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → Data API
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOi...your-anon-or-publishable-key

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL — YouTube Data API v3
#
# Musika is fully functional without this. It buys exactly two things:
#   1. Spotify links can be matched to a YouTube equivalent automatically
#   2. Track durations show in the queue before a track has played
#
# Without it, Spotify links get a friendly "find it on YouTube" screen instead,
# and durations fill in once a track loads.
#
# Restrict it to "Websites (HTTP referrers)" + the YouTube Data API v3 in the
# Google Cloud console. Note honestly: referrer restriction is trivially
# spoofable. It is a quota guard, not a security boundary.
#
# search.list has its own bucket of ~100 calls/day, project-wide.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEXT_PUBLIC_YOUTUBE_API_KEY=AIza...
